/E (Avenue Supermarts has demonstrated a robust expansion in its absolute earnings, with EBITDA growing from 1,634 in March 2019 to 4,494 by March 2025. This trajectory was punctuated by a significant -21.95% contraction in March 2021, followed by a sharp "V-shaped" recovery where growth rates exceeded 30% for two consecutive years in 2022 and 2023. This performance underscores the company's strong operational core, allowing it to nearly triple its absolute EBITDA within six years despite large-scale economic disruptions.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [3]
